---
Implement phaser effect (allpass filter sweep).

Classic phaser using cascaded allpass filters with LFO modulation.
Creates the characteristic sweeping comb filter sound.

## Parameters
- rate: LFO frequency (0.05-5 Hz, default 0.5)
- depth: Sweep range (0-1, default 0.7)
- feedback: Output fed back to input (0-0.95, default 0.5)
- stages: Number of allpass stages (2-12, default 6)
- wet: Wet/dry mix (0-1, default 0.5)

## Implementation
- N cascaded first-order allpass filters
- LFO modulates allpass cutoff frequencies
- Logarithmic frequency sweep (200-4000 Hz range)

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] EFFECT_PHASER added to effect type enum
- [ ] Sweeping notch/peak pattern audible
- [ ] Feedback increases resonance at notch points
- [ ] Stage count changes character of effect

## Test Plan
- [ ] Verify sweep is audible on broadband signal
- [ ] Verify no instability at max feedback
